# Compose UI Components

## Using Common.kt Composables

- **REQUIRED**: When creating composables, ALWAYS prioritize using a defined composable from `Common.kt` (`Common.kt`).
- **REQUIRED**: Before creating a new composable, check if a suitable composable already exists in `Common.kt`.
- **REQUIRED**: Only create new composables if no existing composable in `Common.kt` meets the requirements.

## Common.kt Composable Reference Guide

**Image:** `VectorImage`, `DrawableImage`, `DrawableVectorImage`

**Text:** `TextHeader` — section headers

**Buttons:** `ButtonPositive` (primary/filled), `ButtonNeutral` (outlined), `FlatButton` (text-only uppercase), `FlatButtonNeutral` (transparent)

**Navigation/App Bar:** `Toolbar`, `ToolbarActionQuickView`

**Cards:** `CommonCard`, `CommonCardButton`, `CommonOutlinedCardButton`

**Input:** `InputField`, `PasswordInputField`, `FilterBar`, `CommonSearchBar`

**Lists:** `FilteredList` — searchable list with filter bar and lazy list

**Items/Rows:** `CommonItem`, `CommonItemWithoutPadding`, `CommonSwitch`

**Feedback:** `SnackbarPresenter`, `ErrorBubble`, `WarningBanner`, `CriticalBanner`

**Loading:** `InfiniteLoadingImage`

**Actions:** `ActionFAB` (extended FAB), `ActionButton`

**Other:** `LabelChip`, `DefaultArrowIcon`, `RightModalDrawer`, `UnsupportedDeviceInformation`

```kotlin
// ✅ CORRECT - Using Common.kt composables
@Composable
fun MyScreen() {
    Column {
        TextHeader(text = "Settings")
        ButtonPositive(text = "Save", onClick = { /* ... */ })
        InputField(inputValue = state, label = "Name")
    }
}

// ❌ INCORRECT - Reinventing what Common.kt already provides
@Composable
fun MyScreen() {
    Column {
        Text(text = "Settings", style = MaterialTheme.typography.headlineSmall) // Use TextHeader
        Button(onClick = { /* ... */ }) { Text("Save") } // Use ButtonPositive
        TextField(value = state.value, onValueChange = { /* ... */ }) // Use InputField
    }
}
```
